# ============================================================
# .cursorrules — Spec App Monorepo (Root)
# ============================================================
# This file is read by Cursor before every prompt.
# Each app has its own .cursorrules for app-specific rules.
# ============================================================

## Project Overview
SpecBuilder — Specification Clarification Application.
Workflow-based AI system that converts Minutes of Meeting (MOM)
into structured specification documents with ambiguity/risk detection.
Not a chat AI. AI is only called in controlled workflow steps.
Target users: Business Analysts (BA) and Project Managers (PM).
2 developers. Pre-production / university project + talent competition.

## Monorepo Structure
```
spec-app/
  backend/          → NestJS API + SQS worker
  frontend/         → Next.js web app (Vercel)
  mobile/           → React Native review-only app
  packages/
    schemas/        → shared Zod schemas (@spec-app/schemas)
```

## App Responsibilities

### backend/
- REST API (HTTP)
- SQS worker (async AI generation)
- Two entry points: main.ts (API) and worker.main.ts (worker)
- Owns database, business logic, AI calls, file storage

### frontend/
- Web UI for BA/PM users
- Full workflow: create template, import MOM, generate spec, review
- Currently demo mode (mock data, no real API calls)

### mobile/
- Review-only interface
- Login, view specs, view risks, update status to Reviewed
- Cannot create templates, generate specs, or regenerate

### packages/schemas/
- Shared Zod schemas used by frontend, mobile, and backend validation
- Single source of truth for all DTOs and validation rules
- Never duplicate schemas in individual apps
- Import as @spec-app/schemas

## Tech Stack Summary
- Backend:    NestJS, TypeScript, TypeORM, PostgreSQL 16
- Frontend:   Next.js 16.2 (App Router), Tailwind CSS v4, HeroUI
- Mobile:     React Native
- Shared:     Zod schemas (@spec-app/schemas)
- Queue:      AWS SQS
- AI:         OpenAI API (gpt-4o-mini)
- Storage:    AWS S3
- Secrets:    AWS Secrets Manager
- CI/CD:      GitHub Actions → ECR → ECS Fargate
- Frontend:   Vercel

## Cross-App Rules
- Zod schemas live in packages/schemas only — never duplicated in apps
- Types are inferred from Zod schemas — no manual type duplication
- Backend owns all business logic — frontend/mobile never implement business rules
- Language values: 'EN' | 'TH' (code) — consistent across all apps
- Spec is read-only after generation — no editing in any app
- Regenerate always creates a new version — never mutates existing

## Separation of Concerns
- Do NOT suggest backend changes when working in frontend/
- Do NOT suggest frontend changes when working in backend/
- Do NOT duplicate Zod schemas outside packages/schemas/
- Do NOT implement business logic in frontend or mobile
- Do NOT make real API calls from frontend until after demo
